    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/scholarship-oversight-and-enrollment-finance-manager-531027-tuscaloosa-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Scholarship Oversight and Enrollment Finance Manager - 531027",
      "description": "Scholarship Oversight and Enrollment Finance Manager - 531027 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode Scholarship Oversight and Enrollment Finance Manager - 531027 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Scholarship Oversight and Enrollment Finance Manager - 531027 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Accounting/Bookkeeping Management/General Business Other Closing at: Nov 11 2026 - 22:55 CST Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $69,200 - Midpoint: $89,900 (Salaried E11) Department/Organization: 200601 - VP Enrollment Management Normal Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8:00am to 5:00pm Note to Applicants: Position is eligible for hybrid work subject to University policy . Job Summary: The Scholarship Oversight and Enrollment Finance Manager provides advanced scholarship oversight, fund utilization monitoring, operational budget support, financial reporting, and financial data management for Enrollment Management. Assists with the development and implementation of processes for endowed scholarship oversight, including reconciliation coordination, data reporting standards, fund utilization review, spending plan support, and scholarship awarding system support. Supports Enrollment Management and the Capstone Center for Student Success budget operations by performing detailed review, tracking key financial activity, improving reporting structures, and preparing analyses that support strategic decision-making by the Executive Director and senior leadership. Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree and four (4) years of scholarship and/or financial experience; OR master's degree and two (2) years of scholarship and/or financial experience. Skills and Knowledge: Strong budgetary, supervisory, and communication skills. Ability to perform complex financial analyses, including scholarship budgeting. Ability to develop reports, review data across systems, identify discrepancies, and translate information into actionable recommendations. Preferred Qualifications: Experience at a complex R1 university. Experience with financial aid and scholarship analysis. Familiarity with donor-funded scholarship programs. Experience with scholarship administration, restricted or donor-funded resources, higher education budgeting, reconciliation coordination, reporting, data management, or complex fund oversight. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportunity : The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to any legally protected basis and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. More information is available in the EEOC’s Know Your Rights: Workplace discrimination is illegal poster. The University of Alabama affirms its longstanding commitment to institutional neutrality, free speech, and academic freedom. Apply Now REGISTER FOR JOB ALERTS: First Name (required) 3be7741f Last Name (required) e1090fac Email (required) b45