    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/school-student-recruitment-coordinator-530880-tuscaloosa-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "School Student Recruitment Coordinator - 530880",
      "description": "School Student Recruitment Coordinator - 530880 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode School Student Recruitment Coordinator - 530880 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search School Student Recruitment Coordinator - 530880 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Administrative / Professional Communication Closing at: Nov 10 2026 - 22:55 CST Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $44,600 - Midpoint: $55,800 (Salaried E6) Department/Organization: 224102 - Social Work Normal Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8:00am to 5:00pm; some evenings & weekends as necessary Job Summary: The School Student Recruitment Coordinator organizes and coordinates the recruitment operations for the school. Seeks out potential candidates by representing the school at high schools, community colleges, and professional association gatherings. Coordinates and/or delivers the school's presentations at campus recruitment events. Develops and executes initiatives focused on enhancing student recruitment rates. Additional Department Summary: Plays a key role within the admissions and recruitment team in the School of Social Work, which manages the student recruitment and admissions process from point-of-inquiry through enrollment for the school's undergraduate and graduate programs. Develops and conducts information sessions, both on and off campus. Responds to telephone and electronic requests for information. Plans and delivers presentations to potential students within and outside of the state. Plans and organizes student-focused events. Serves as a point of contact for university department chairs and high school guidance counselors in Alabama and neighboring states. Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree or higher. Additional Required Department Minimum Qualifications: Must have valid U.S. driver's license. Must be at least 19 years of age at time of hire and have an acceptable Motor Vehicle Report that is in compliance with University policies. Applicants under the age of 21 will have some driving restrictions. Skills and Knowledge: Familiarity with current research regarding student admissions, recruitment, and enrollment management. Ability to use Microsoft applications and other student information systems at a practitioner level, as well as utilize new recruitment/admissions technologies to increase efficiency and reach. Ability to serve as an articulate spokesperson for the mission and values of the School of Social Work. Strong project management skills. Ability to think, reason, and make sound judgments on how responsibilities are completed in compliance with school and university standards. Ability to work with various groups of people. A high degree of professionalism, discretion, and judgment. Excellent communication, presentation, interpersonal, organizational, and computer skills, including proficiency with related systems and databases. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in social work and two (2) years post master's experience. Experience in student services and recruitment in higher education or experience in administration. Expertise in using electronic software to plan and schedule events and activities; to organize and interpret information, and to provide instruction. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individ