    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/student-engagement-and-transfer-initiatives-program-manager-531000-tuscaloosa-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Student Engagement and Transfer Initiatives Program Manager - 531000",
      "description": "Student Engagement and Transfer Initiatives Program Manager - 531000 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode Student Engagement and Transfer Initiatives Program Manager - 531000 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Student Engagement and Transfer Initiatives Program Manager - 531000 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Administrative / Professional Closing at: Nov 10 2026 - 22:55 CST Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $54,000 - Midpoint: $67,500 (Salaried E8) Department/Organization: 200673 - CCSS-Stud Academic Engag & Advocacy Normal Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8:00am to 5:00pm; some nights and weekends as needed. Job Summary: The Student Engagement and Transfer Initiatives Program Manager advances campus engagement for new and continuing main-campus transfer students. Directs transfer student engagement initiatives and serves a point of contact for main-campus transfer students in their academic and social transition and experiences at The University of Alabama. Works to address gaps in retention, persistence, and graduation for transfer students. Develops and maintains a strong portfolio of programmatic events and resources specific to transfer student success. Oversees the online presence for transfer student initiatives by maintaining the Transfer Programs website and producing social media content that aligns with the goals of the office. Supports ongoing engagement initiatives for the overall Office of Student Academic Engagement & Advocacy. Additional Department Summary: Coordinates data collection and assessment efforts to better understand the transfer student population and uses quantitative and qualitative findings to inform decision-making, program development, and continuous improvement. Builds collaborative campus partnerships, oversees communication and digital engagement efforts, and advocates for the academic, social, and involvement needs of transfer students. Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree and four (4) years of student retention or engagement experience; OR master's degree and two (2) years of student retention or engagement experience. Skills and Knowledge: Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Excellent social, digital, and interactive media content development skills. Strong organizational and relationship-building skills. Ability to work effectively with students, faculty, and staff in a collaborative manner. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in Higher Education or related field. Experience in communications, marketing, and/or coordinating programs for first-year students. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportunity : The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to any legally protected basis and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. More information is available in the EEOC’s Know Your Rights: Workplace discrimination is i