      "title": "Painter I - 531036",
      "description": "Painter I - 531036 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode Painter I - 531036 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Painter I - 531036 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Facilities/ Grounds Maintenance/Skilled Trades/Service Closing at: Nov 6 2026 - 22:55 CST Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $19.52 - Midpoint: $24.38 (Hourly N5) Department/Organization: 504241 - Building Maintenance Normal Work Schedule: Varies; May include evening and nights Job Summary: The Painter I performs routine preparation and staining or painting of interior and exterior surfaces. Must drive from site to site. Required Minimum Qualifications: Two (2) years of construction trades experience to include one (1) year in painting. Additional Required Department Minimum Qualifications: Must have valid U.S. driver's license. Must be at least 19 years of age at time of hire and have an acceptable Motor Vehicle Report that is in compliance with University policies. Applicants under the age of 21 will have some driving restrictions. Final candidates must submit to and successfully pass a post-offer drug screen. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportu