    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/communications-program-manager-530123-tuscaloosa-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Communications Program Manager - 530123",
      "description": "Communications Program Manager - 530123 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode Communications Program Manager - 530123 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Communications Program Manager - 530123 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Communication Other Closing at: Nov 6 2026 - 22:55 CST Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $57,200 - Midpoint: $74,300 (Salaried E9) Department/Organization: 215101 - Dean's Office-Graduate School Normal Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8:00am to 5:00pm Note to Applicants: Position is eligible for hybrid work subject to University policy . Job Summary: The Communications Program Manager oversees strategic communications for the college including all college-level print materials, digital content, and social media. Uses analytics and reports to inform and guide communications and campaigns. Additional Department Summary: Leads strategic communications and marketing for the Graduate School. Develops communications and campaigns that grow graduate recruitment, enrollment, and advance the Graduate School’s strategic priorities. Plans and executes recruitment and enrollment marketing. Manages the Graduate School’s brand and web and social presence. Produces communications that engage current graduate students and the campus community. Works closely with the Dean on messaging and executive communications. Partners with Strategic Communications to promote the Graduate School and its people. Supervises student assistants who support the work. Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree and six (6) years of journalism, public relations, marketing, or communications experience; OR master's degree and four (4) years of journalism, public relations, marketing, or communications experience. Skills and Knowledge: Proficiency in computer skills and AP Style. Exceptional written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Demonstrated project management, strategic thinking, and leadership skills. Understanding of website content management (e.g., WordPress) and information design and management. Social media management, email marketing, and basic graphic design (e.g., Adobe Creative Suite or Canva) skills. Ability to use web and campaign analytics to guide decisions. Preferred Qualifications: Experience managing media relations. Experience in higher-education marketing or recruitment communications. Graphic design, photography/videography, or web/CMS production experience. Experience running social media and email-marketing campaigns and interpreting their analytics. Familiarity with a CRM (e.g., Slate) for prospective-student communications. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportunity : The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to any legally protected basis and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. More information is available in the EEOC’s Know Your Rights: Workplace discrimination is illegal poster. The University of Alabama affirms its longstanding commitment to institutional neutrality, free speech, and academic freedom. Apply Now REGISTER FOR JOB ALERTS: First Name (required) 6d072f26 Last Name (required) 483fbbfb Email (required) c10cae95 Select from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs. e383bf42 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Communication Other Communication Other Employment Type Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) Submit Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! EMAIL THIS JOB TO A FRIEND: First Name (required) 1aff034e Last Name (required) 57629d1e Email (required) a7abf2c7 Friend's Information f70ef470 Share Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for sharing! Please note- all Employment positions close at 10:55pm CST. Non-Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 3 days. Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 7 days. Faculty positions are posted a minimum of 30 days. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 4ac0c558 Last Name (required) 6862ce65 Email (required) 9d8f7659 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you, you will now be taken to the application. Need help? Please email the Human Resources Department at hr@ua.edu or contact us by phone at (205)-348-7732. If you anticipate needing any type of accommodation to participate in any portion of the University's employment process, including completion of the online application process, please contact our office in advance of your participation or visit. Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status withou