    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/nursing-supervisor-umc-obgyn-clinics-531016-tuscaloosa-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Nursing Supervisor - UMC OBGYN Clinics - 531016",
      "description": "Nursing Supervisor - UMC OBGYN Clinics - 531016 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode Nursing Supervisor - UMC OBGYN Clinics - 531016 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Nursing Supervisor - UMC OBGYN Clinics - 531016 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Health Care / Social Services Other Closing at: Nov 9 2026 - 22:55 CST Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $69,200 - Midpoint: $89,900 (Salaried E11) Department/Organization: 208444 - UMC OB/GYN Normal Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8:00am to 5:00pm; some early morning/evening/weekend hours as needed Job Summary: The Nursing Supervisor provides administrative direction, supervision, and management of the nursing services to ensure quality patient care and treatment. Provides treatment to patients within the scope of their license assisting physicians and nurse practitioners with patient care. Additional Department Summary: Supervises daily clinical operations and patient care for University Medical Center OBGYN Clinics located in Tuscaloosa, AL and Fayette, AL. Under the leadership and direction of the Assistant Director of UMC Nursing Services and Chief Nursing Officer, oversees and coordinates daily clinic operations to ensure the delivery of high-quality, patient-centered care. Collaborates closely with clinic Medical Directors and providers to support the effective management of clinical services and promote the patient-centered medical home model of care. Maintains strict confidentiality of protected health information and ensures compliance with all HIPAA and organizational privacy requirements. Provides direct supervision of clinical staff, including nurses, medical assistants, scribes, and other support personnel. Assists in the development, implementation, and enforcement of clinic policies, procedures, and standards of practice. Delivers ongoing leadership, coaching, and training to foster a high-performing clinical team and cultivate a culture of accountability, professionalism, integrity, and service excellence. Oversees staffing schedules, workforce planning, onboarding, training, competency development, and performance management activities. Partners with clinic Medical Directors, faculty, and providers to support educational and clinical learning experiences for medical students, residents, fellows, and other learners, helping to ensure they acquire the knowledge, skills, and professional competencies necessary for future success. Promotes continuous quality improvement, operational efficiency, and exceptional patient experiences while performing all responsibilities in alignment with the University’s mission, values, and principles. Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree and four (4) years of LPN or RN experience to include one (1) year of supervisory experience; OR associate's degree and six (6) years of LPN or RN experience to include one (1) year of supervisory experience Additional Required Department Minimum Qualifications: Must be at least 19 years of age at time of hire and have an acceptable Motor Vehicle Report that is in compliance with university policies. Applicants under the age of 21 will have some driving restrictions. Final candidates must submit to and successfully pass a post-offer drug screen. Skills and Knowledge: Ability to perform patient care as directed by a physician, nurse practitioner, or other qualified medical professional. Working knowledge of electronic health record (EHR) systems and proficiency in computer applications, data entry, and documentation. Strong verbal and written communication, customer service, public relations, and telephone etiquette skills. Ability to effectively prioritize and manage multiple responsibilities in a fast-paced clinical environment. Ability to exercise sound judgment, discretion, diplomacy, and tact when interacting with patients, families, providers, and staff. Commitment to continuous learning and professional development, with a demonstrated ability to deliver high-quality, patient-centered, and service-oriented care. Strong organizational, problem-solving, and teamwork skills, with the ability to adapt to changing priorities and operational needs. Demonstrated punctuality and reliability, with the flexibility to work extended hours as needed to support clinic operations and meet patient care needs. Preferred Qualifications: Current CPR certification. Prior experience working as a member of an interdisciplinary treatment team in a primary care ambulatory healthcare setting. Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively with providers, nursing staff, and other healthcare professionals to support coordinated, patient-centered care and achieve positive clinical outcomes. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportunity : The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to any legally protected basis and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. More information is available in the EEOC’s Know Your Rights: Workplace discrimination is illegal poster. The University of Alabama affirms its longstanding commitment to institutional neutrality, free speech, and academic freedom. Apply Now REGISTER FOR JOB ALERTS: First Name (required) c505cc76 Last Name (required) 9da4348a Email (required) c5b9d44f Select from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs. a4bba64c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Health Care / Social Services Other Health Care / Social Services Other Employment Type Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) Submit Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! EMAIL THIS JOB TO A FRIEND: First Name (required) f07890d4 Last Name (required) 44480270 Email (required) b2349018 Friend's Information a5ccba00 Share Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for sharing! Please note- all Employment positions close at 10:55pm CST. Non-Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 3 days. Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 7 days. Faculty positions are posted a minimum of 30 days. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 628fc1ff Last Name (required) 67ef3ed0 Email (required) e4f4b90a Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you, you will now be taken to the application. Need help? Please email the Human Resources Department at hr@ua.edu or contact us by phone at (205)-348-7732. If you anticipate needing any type of accommodation to participate in any portion of the University's employment process, including completion of the online application process, please contact our office in advance of your participation or visit. Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, age, genetic or family medical history information, disability, protected veteran status, or any other legally protected basis, and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants to and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. Pay Transparency Policy Statement The contractor will not discharge or in any other manner discriminate against employees or applicants because they have inquired about, discussed, or disclosed their own pay or the pay of another employee or applicant. However, employees who have access to the compensation information of other employees or applicants as a part of their essential job functions cannot disclose the pay of other employees or applicants to individuals who do not otherwise have access to compensation information, unless the disclosure is (a) in response to a formal complaint or charge, (b) in furtherance of an investigation, proceeding, hearing, or action, including an investigation conducted by the employer, or (c) consistent with the contractor’s legal duty to furnish information. Supplemental Links EEOC Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Polygraph Protection Act The University of Alabama Annual Campus Security and Fire Safety Report contains information on campus safety statistics as well as University Safety and Security Policies. The report is available online to view or print at safety.ua.edu . FOLLOW US Accessibility | Equal Opportunity | About This Site | Webmaster Copyright © 2021 The University of Alabama | Disclaimer | Privacy | Accessibility Candidate Details × This website uses cookies to collect information to improve your browsi