    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/assistant-manager-grounds-530998-tuscaloosa-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager Grounds - 530998",
      "description": "Assistant Manager Grounds - 530998 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode Assistant Manager Grounds - 530998 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Assistant Manager Grounds - 530998 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Facilities/ Grounds Closing at: Nov 10 2026 - 22:55 CST Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $57,200 - Midpoint: $74,300 (Salaried E9) Department/Organization: 504103 - Grounds Normal Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 6:00am to 2:30pm; includes some nights, weekends, and campus events Job Summary: The Assistant Manager of Grounds manages, schedules, and assigns work for Laborers, Groundskeepers, Team Leads, Truck Drivers, and Equipment Operators. Provides customer service by interacting with customers to clarify work orders, set work schedules, and follow up during and at completion of work. Conducts on-site inspections for work in progress and completed work projects. Additional Department Summary: Required to work additional hours as needed, some after-hour special events, all home football game weekends, and on-call weekends. Must be able to work in all types of weather conditions. Required Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or GED and eight (8) years of groundskeeping experience; OR associate's degree and six (6) years of groundskeeping experience; OR bachelor's degree and four (4) years of groundskeeping experience; OR master's degree and two (2) years of groundskeeping experience. Additional Required Department Minimum Qualifications: Must have valid U.S. driver's license. Must be at least 19 years of age at time of hire and have an acceptable Motor Vehicle Report that is in compliance with University policies. Applicants under the age of 21 will have some driving restrictions. Final candidates must submit to and successfully pass a post-offer drug screen. Skills and Knowledge: Must be able to lift, handle and maneuver the tools, materials and supplies of the job. Ability to read and interpret blueprints, schematics, and plans. Basic knowledge of Microsoft Office products and enterprise management systems. Ability to effectively use systems for scheduling personnel and inventory, purchasing, communicating, and reporting. Ability to perform inspections. Good verbal and written communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: Alabama Ornamental and Turf Pesticide Applicator certification or ability to obtain certification within six (6) months of hire. Degree in landscape horticulture, architecture, construction, business management, or similarly related field of study. Understanding of work-related Spanish communication. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportunity : The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to any legally protected basis and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. More information is available in the EEOC’s Know Your Rights: Workplace discrimination 