    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/geochemical-laboratory-coordinator-530923-tuscaloosa-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Geochemical Laboratory Coordinator - 530923",
      "description": "Geochemical Laboratory Coordinator - 530923 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode Geochemical Laboratory Coordinator - 530923 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Geochemical Laboratory Coordinator - 530923 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Other Research/Scientific Closing at: Nov 20 2026 - 22:55 CST Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $54,000 - Midpoint: $67,500 (Salaried E8) Department/Organization: 204441 - Geological Sciences Normal Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8:00am to 5:00pm Job Summary: The Geochemical Laboratory Coordinator assists in determining and implementing the analytical requirements of the faculty and graduate students in the Department of Geological Sciences, as well as other departments and colleges. Works closely with faculty and students to accomplish timely, accurate, and precise analyses of aqueous samples using chromatographic (IC) and spectroscopic (ICP-OES, ICP-MS, GFAA) techniques. Additional Department Summary: Supports the Geological Elemental Analysis Laboratory (GEAL), with primary responsibility for inorganic chemical, trace-element, and isotope analysis of aqueous and solid samples. The position operates and maintains ICP-OES, ion chromatography, ICP-MS/LA-ICP-MS, and microwave digestion systems; prepares and analyzes samples; develops and validates analytical methods; manages quality-control records; supports laboratory safety and organization; and trains and assists laboratory users. Required Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in geochemistry, analytical chemistry, geology/earth science, environmental chemistry/science, or a closely related field and two (2) years of laboratory experience; OR doctorate in geochemistry, analytical chemistry, geology/earth science, environmental chemistry/science, or a closely related field and some laboratory experience. Skills and Knowledge: Knowledge of ICP-MS, laser-ablation ICP-MS, ICP-OES, ion chromatography, and related analytical workflows; instrument calibration, tuning, maintenance, and troubleshooting; microwave-assisted acid digestion and other sample-preparation methods; trace-element and isotope analysis; analytical method development and validation; QA/QC and data management; chemical hygiene, PPE, waste management, laboratory safety, inventory, and instrument scheduling. Preferred Qualifications: Hands-on experience operating and maintaining advanced geochemical analytical instrumentation, especially ICP-MS, LA-ICP-MS, ICP-OES, and ion chromatographs. Experience with trace-element or isotope analysis, analytical method development, QA/QC, scientific data interpretation, laboratory safety/compliance, and training students or other laboratory users is preferred. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportunity : The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to any legally protected basis and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimi