    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/high-performance-computing-data-storage-administrator-iv-530901-tuscaloosa-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "High Performance Computing Data Storage Administrator IV - 530901",
      "description": "High Performance Computing Data Storage Administrator IV - 530901 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode High Performance Computing Data Storage Administrator IV - 530901 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search High Performance Computing Data Storage Administrator IV - 530901 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Information Systems/Technology Support Closing at: Nov 5 2026 - 22:55 CST Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $94,700 - Midpoint: $127,900 (Salaried E14) Department/Organization: 200706 - OIT-HPC Center Services Normal Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8:00am to 5:00pm Note to Applicants: Position is eligible for hybrid work subject to University policy . Job Summary: The High Performance Computing Data Storage Administrator IV designs and administers enterprise and high-performance computing (HPC) storage systems. Establishes long-term strategies for storage technology and services. Develops storage roadmaps and leads modernization initiatives. Architects large-scale parallel filesystem environments. Analyzes large-scale input/output workloads and establishes infrastructure-as-code strategies to automate provisioning, monitoring, capacity reporting, lifecycle management, and disaster recovery. Leads enterprise-scale integration of storage environments with cloud platforms, archival consortia, external research collaborations, and multi-site infrastructure. Forecasts storage growth and research demand and establishes expansion strategies. Defines storage security and encryption strategies for complex and regulated research environments. Mentors storage administrators and provides technical leadership through presentations and training. Additional Department Summary: Serves as the principle technical and operational lead responsible for designing, implementing, optimizing, and operating the University's high-performance research storage infrastructure. Provides design leadership for multi-petabyte storage systems supporting HPC, AI, machine learning, and data-intensive research. May lead a team of High Performance Computing Data Storage Administrators. Partners with systems, networking, cybersecurity, cloud, and research application teams to deliver scalable, resilient, and high-performance storage services. Contributes to shaping the future direction of the University's research cyberinfrastructure. Required Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or GED and ten (10) years of systems administration or storage administration experience; OR associate's degree and eight (8) years of systems administration or storage administration experience; OR bachelor's degree six (6) years of systems administration or storage administration experience; OR master's degree and four (4) years of systems administration or storage administration experience. Additional Required Department Minimum Qualifications: Must have valid U.S. driver's license. Must be at least 19 years of age at time of hire and have an acceptable Motor Vehicle Report that is in compliance with University policies. Applicants under the age of 21 will have some driving restrictions. Skills and Knowledge: Strong scripting or software development skills. Excellent communication and project leadership skills. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in computer science, information systems, data science, or a related computational discipline. Five (5) or more years of experience designing and administering enterprise or HPC storage systems. Experience in research computing IT for national laboratories (connectivity/use/researcher support). Experience supporting AI infrastructure. Experience with GPU clusters. Experience integrating storage with SLURM. Experience with cloud storage design. Experience with object storage. Experience with vendor platforms such as DDN, VAST Data, Dell PowerScale, or NetApp. Extensive Linux administration experience. Experience with one or more parallel filesystems. Experience supporting multi-petabyte storage environments. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportunity : The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to any legally protected basis and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. More information is available in the EEOC’s Know Your Rights: Workplace discrimination is illegal poster. The University of Alabama affirms its longstanding commitment to institutional neutrality, free speech, and academic freedom. Apply Now REGISTER FOR JOB ALERTS: First Name (required) 5e056a32 Last Name (required) 333330af Email (required) 4d80b012 Select from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs. cc906460 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Information Syste