      "description": "BCAS - Assistant Professor of Public Administration, in Political Science - 530397 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode BCAS - Assistant Professor of Public Administration, in Political Science - 530397 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search BCAS - Assistant Professor of Public Administration, in Political Science - 530397 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Arts and Sciences Tenure/Tenure-Track Faculty Closing at: Aug 1 2027 - 22:55 CDT Department/Organization 204691 - Political Science Rank Assistant Professor Position Summary The Department of Political Science invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Public Administration, beginning August 16, 2027. Detailed Position Information The Department of Political Science invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Public Administration, beginning August 16, 2027. The successful candidate will take an active role in the department’s graduate Master of Public Administration (MPA) program and contribute to undergraduate teaching. While we welcome applicants from all subfields of public administration, we are particularly interested in candidates with research and teaching interests in public budgeting, financial management, or nonprofit management. Review of applications will begin on September 21, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. For more information, please contact the search committee chair, Hyunjung Ji, at hji4@ua.edu. Minimum Qualifications A completed Ph.D. in public administration, public policy, political science, or a closely related field is required at the time of appointment. Candidates should demonstrate a strong research agenda with 