    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/accounting-assistant-iii-531089-tuscaloosa-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Accounting Assistant III - 531089",
      "description": "Accounting Assistant III - 531089 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode Accounting Assistant III - 531089 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Accounting Assistant III - 531089 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Accounting/Bookkeeping Closing at: Nov 16 2026 - 22:55 CST Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $19.52 - Midpoint: $24.38 (Hourly N5) Department/Organization: 502702 - Campus Financial Affairs Normal Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8:00am to 5:00pm Job Summary: The Accounting Assistant III maintains accurate financial records. Provides accounting and bookkeeping support. Assists University staff in understanding industry standards, current laws, and university policy as it relates to the financial affairs of the University. Provides guidance, trains, and/or may supervise entry-level Accounting Assistants. Additional Department Summary: Serves as the primary financial contact for the department of Information Systems, Statistics, and Management Science (ISM) in the Culverhouse College of Business. Provides advanced financial support to the Department Chair. Maintains department budgets. Submits payroll forms for processing. Submits faculty requisitions in PageUp for the department. Required Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or GED and four (4) years of accounting or bookkeeping experience; OR associate's degree and two (2) years of accounting or bookkeeping experience; OR bachelor's degree. Skills and Knowledge: General knowledge of accounting principles. Ability to multi-task, prioritize, and make decisions independently. Knowledge of Microsoft Word and Excel. Understanding of UA systems and processes, including eTime, Everest, Banner/ePrint, PageUp, Touchnet, Concur, purchasing card policies and procedures, and onboarding for new employees. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportunity : The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to any legally protected basis and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. More information is available in the EEOC’s Know Your Rights: Workplace discrimination is illegal poster. The University of Alabama affirms its longstanding commitment to institutional neutrality, free speech, and academic freedom. Apply Now Please note- all Employment positions close at 10:55pm CST. Non-Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 3 days. Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 7 days. Faculty positions are posted a minimum of 30 days. Need help? Please email the Human Resources Department at hr@ua.edu or contact us by phone at (205)-348-7732. If you anticipate needing any type of accommodation to participate in any portion of the University's employment process, including completion of the online application process, please contact our office in advance of your participation or visit. Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Alabama is an Equal Employme