hapter policies. Holds staff accountable for completing required training and following established operational, safety, and service standards. Completes all required training and promotes a safe, hospitable, and respectful residential environment. Works collaboratively with House Corporation leadership, University departments, vendors, and other partners to ensure facility and residential operations comply with applicable University, organizational, local, health, life-safety, and security requirements. Serves as a consistent resource and primary point of contact for residents, House Corporation representatives, alumni/ae, volunteers, parents, vendors, University officials, and other external constituents. Promotes a positive residential experience by fostering an engaging and receptive community, participating in resident meals and chapter functions, and communicating expectations, house needs, and operational practices. Maintains regular accessibility to address operational needs and respond to emergencies and critical incidents, including following established emergency procedures to notify appropriate local authorities and University officials and provide direction to staff while maintaining a resident-focused approach. Participates in Fraternity & Sorority Life training and meetings, contributes to assessment and continuous improvement of the residential experience, and conducts and documents routine safety checks and required reporting. Required Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or GED. Skills and Knowledge: Good judgment skills. Familiarity with University and community resources. Knowledge of computers and software ( Microsoft Excel and Word, e-mail, etc.). Demonstrates commitment to supporting all students. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as 