      "title": "Administrative Assistant II - 531101",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant II - 531101 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode Administrative Assistant II - 531101 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Administrative Assistant II - 531101 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Administrative / Professional Closing at: Nov 13 2026 - 22:55 CST Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $18.46 - Midpoint: $22.16 (Hourly N4) Department/Organization: 212501 - Ed Leadership/Policy/Tech Studies Normal Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8:00am to 5:00pm Job Summary: The Administrative Assistant II provides administrative support for the operations of unit. Performs moderately complex and well documented administrative tasks. Acts as office liaison/receptionist. Receives and routes phone calls, emails, and/or guests. Maintains files and enters data. Drafts and sends communications on supervisor/departmental staff behalf. Reconciles P-Card/Concur for other staff/faculty against departmental budget. Performs some simple budget monitoring/entry. Operates standard office equipment such as personal computers, copiers, fax machines, etc. Additional Department Summary: Provides comprehensive administrative support for the Department of Educational Leadership, Policy, and Technology Studies (ELPTS), serving all program areas, including Educational Leadership (EDLE), Higher Education Administration (HEA), Instructional Technology (IT), and Social and Cultural Studies (SCS). Supports faculty, instructional staff, and students across all programs and serves as a central point of coordination for departmental operations and administrative processes. Performs other duties including financial processing and pre‑approval coordination, faculty hiring and workload support, student services, and general administrative operations in support of program and departmental priorities. Required Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma or GED and two (2) years of administrative experience; OR associate’s degree or higher. Skills and Knowledge: Strong organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines. Attention to detail, particularly in financial documentation and data tracking. Effective written and verbal communication skills. Proficiency with standard office technologies (e.g., Microsoft Office), including the ability to work with spreadsheets and data tracking tools. Ability to work in a fast-paced, interruption-driven environment while maintaining accuracy and consistency. Preferred Qualifications: Experience providing administrative support in a higher education setting, using spreadsheets to organize, track, and maintain data across multiple processes or workflows. Experience with financial and administrative processes (e.g., travel authorizations, reimbursements, supplemental pay). Experience supporting faculty, academic programs, or student services. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportunity : The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to any legally protected basis and will not be d