    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/manager-financial-affairs-531118-tuscaloosa-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Manager Financial Affairs - 531118",
      "description": "Manager Financial Affairs - 531118 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode Manager Financial Affairs - 531118 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Manager Financial Affairs - 531118 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Accounting/Bookkeeping Management/General Business Closing at: Nov 17 2026 - 22:55 CST Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $74,900 - Midpoint: $101,100 (Salaried E12) Department/Organization: 502702 - Campus Financial Affairs Normal Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8:00am to 5:00pm Job Summary: The Manager of Financial Affairs manages day-to-day financial activities for assigned area(s). Applies accounting principles, practices, and techniques in accordance with industry standards, current laws, and University policies. Manages resources and coordinates activities to support departmental goals and objectives. Oversees financial controls and audits. Ensures policy compliance. Leads process improvements. Supervises clerical accounting staff and provides guidance on daily operations, procedures, and assigned responsibilities. Builds strong working relationships with faculty and staff across the college or unit. Assists with strategic financial planning. Additional Department Summary: Works closely with the Director of Financial Affairs II in the Styslinger College of Engineering to provide strategic leadership, oversight, and guidance for the college's financial and administrative operations. Serves as a key advisor to department heads and college leadership on budgeting, fiscal planning, procurement, payroll funding, compliance, and the effective stewardship of financial resources. Manages the development, administration, and monitoring of operating budgets, gifts, endowments, and other funding sources while ensuring compliance with University, state, federal, and sponsor requirements. Leads college-wide financial reporting, analysis, internal controls, reconciliation oversight, audits, fiscal year-end activities, and compliance initiatives to support sound financial management and informed decision-making. Directly supervises and develops departmental financial support staff through hiring, training, performance management, professional development, and succession planning. Working collaboratively with college leadership, departments, central administrative offices, and the college finance team, serves as a resource for resolving complex financial and administrative issues while promoting accurate, timely, and policy-compliant financial administration. Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree or higher in accounting, finance, business, or a related financial field and six (6) years of accounting experience; OR Certified Public Accountant (CPA) and four (4) years of accounting experience. Skills and Knowledge: Strong leadership, supervisory, organizational, and interpersonal skills, with the ability to hire, train, develop, and support staff. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Ability to translate financial requirements into clear procedures and guidance. Knowledge of accounting, budgeting, reconciliation, internal controls, financial reporting, and fiscal year-end processes. Ability to analyze complex financial information, identify discrepancies or risks, develop practical solutions, and communicate recommendations. Ability to manage multiple priorities, meet deadlines, exercise sound judgment, and work effectively in a fast-paced environment with frequent interruptions. Advanced spreadsheet and database skills, including the ability to create and maintain complex tracking tools and management reports. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, department leadership, central offices, and other stakeholders while maintaining confidentiality and exercising appropriate discretion. Knowledge of University financial, accounting, purchasing, payroll, human resources, and sponsored-project policies and systems. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in accounting, finance, business administration, or a closely related field and/or CPA. Six (6) years of experience overseeing financial operations, supervising staff, developing procedures, performing financial reconciliations or audits, and supporting budget administration. Higher education or not-for-profit accounting experience. Experience and familiarity with the University's accounting, budgeting, purchasing, payroll, sponsored-project, and human resources policies and procedures. Experience using Banner, Concur, PageUp, and related University systems. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportunity : The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to any legally protected basis and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. More information is available in the EEOC’s Know Your Rights: Workplace discrimination is illegal poster. The University of Alabama affirms its longstanding commitment to institutional neutrality, free speech, and academic freedom. Apply Now REGISTER FOR JOB ALERTS: First Name (required) fb825682 Last Name (required) 59596e05 Email (required) b1561ab1 Select from the lists below to receive information about specific jobs. 15dcf225 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Accounting/Bookkeeping Management/General Business Accounting/Bookkeeping Management/General Business Employment Type Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) Regular Full-time (Benefits eligible) Submit Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you! EMAIL THIS JOB TO A FRIEND: First Name (required) a52b6945 Last Name (required) 073f1b42 Email (required) abe9cef8 Friend's Information eac4d727 Share Now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you for sharing! Please note- all Employment positions close at 10:55pm CST. Non-Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 3 days. Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 7 days. Faculty positions are posted a minimum of 30 days. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) f2a32fd8 Last Name (required) 2e01a557 Email (required) 95d4e669 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you, you will now be taken to the application. Need help? Please email the Human Resources Department at hr@ua.edu or contact us by phone at (205)-348-7732. If you anticipate needing any type of accommodation to participate in any portion of the University's employment process, including completion of the online application process, please contact our office in advance of your participation or visit. Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, age, genetic or family medical history information, disability, protected veteran status, or any other legally protected basis, and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants to and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. Pay Transparency Policy Statement The contractor will not discharge or in any other manner discriminate against employees or applicants because they have inquired about, discussed, or disclosed their own pay or the pay of another employee or applicant. However, employees who have access to the compensation information of other employees or applicants as a part of their essential job functions cannot disclose the pay of other employees or applicants to individuals who do not otherwise have access to compensation information, unless the disclosure is (a) in response to a formal complaint or charge, (b) in furtherance of an investigation, proceeding, hearing, or action, including an investigation conducted by the employer, or (c) consistent with the contractor’s legal duty to furnish information. Supplemental Links EEOC Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Polygraph Protection Act The University of Alabama Annual Campus Security and Fire Safety Report contains information on campus safety statistics as well as University Safety and Security Policies. The report is available online to view or print at safety.ua.edu . FOLLOW US Accessibility | Equal Opportunity | About This Site | Webmaster Copyright © 2021 The University of Alabama | Disclaimer | Privacy | Accessibility Candidate Details × This website uses cookies to collect information to improve your browsing experience. Please review our Privacy Statement for more information. I do not accept I accept Please choose the employment type(s)"
