    "https://careers.ua.edu/jobs/accountant-iii-cchs-finance-office-531147-tuscaloosa-alabama-united-states": {
      "title": "Accountant III - CCHS Finance Office - 531147",
      "description": "Accountant III - CCHS Finance Office - 531147 - Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States My settings Featured Jobs Research Healthcare Information Technology (IT) Life at UA Campus Life Tuscaloosa Benefits Work Life Search Jobs Job Alerts Staff Jobs Student Jobs Faculty Jobs UA System Jobs My Application Kiosk mode Accountant III - CCHS Finance Office - 531147 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Apply Now Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Accountant III - CCHS Finance Office - 531147 Tuscaloosa, Alabama, United States Accounting/Bookkeeping Other Closing at: Nov 23 2026 - 22:55 CST Pay Grade/Pay Range: Minimum: $57,200 - Midpoint: $74,300 (Salaried E9) Department/Organization: 502702 - Campus Financial Affairs Normal Work Schedule: Monday - Friday 8:00am to 5:00pm; occasional evening/weekend hours as needed Job Summary: The Accountant III prepares, reconciles, and audits budgets under minimal supervision. Prepares financial reports, invoices, schedules, and/or statements. Completes journal entries. Reviews, analyzes, and approves expenditures. Determines fund balances. Ensures compliance with applicable laws, University policies, and procedures. Provides guidance, trains, and/or may supervise entry-level accountants. Additional Department Summary: Serves as a financial and budget liaison to a variety of departments within the College of Community Health Sciences (CCHS). Assists with managing all fiscal operations, including budget development and administration, fiscal accountability, financial planning, and resource management to maximize the effective use of departmental and organizational resources. Performs a variety of complex administrative, financial, and accounting functions, including budget analysis, forecasting, auditing, strategic planning, financial modeling, and other related activities to ensure fiscal integrity, operational efficiency, and compliance with institutional policies and procedures. Assists with managing financial and accounting services for the Capstone Health Services Foundation (CHSF), including accounts payable, accounts receivable, payroll, employee benefit plans, inventory and asset management, and general ledger operations. Partners with the Director of Financial Affairs to provide financial leadership and coordination across CCHS enterprise services, including collaboration with medical billing, compliance, purchasing, health IT, human resources, and other administrative and operational units to support the academic, clinical, research, and business functions of the college and foundation. Performs research and develops financial and operational reporting to support academic, clinical, scholarly, and research enterprises. Ensures the integrity of financial reporting systems, data reporting systems, operational reporting systems, and accreditation reporting processes. Performs all aspects of accounting, financial reporting, cash management, and data reporting functions, while ensuring the timely and accurate preparation of financial analyses and reports for leadership decision-making. Performs salary budget processes, departmental budget reporting, routine monthly, quarterly, and annual reconciliations, financial statement preparation, and financial forecasting. Provides oversight for all aspects of state budget accounting processes, including Banner and Concur review, reconciliation, compliance, and reporting. Follows, enforces, and assists in the development and continuous improvement of internal processes, control policies, and operating procedures in compliance with University of Alabama, CCHS, SHC, and CHSF policies, as well as applicable financial, regulatory, and audit requirements. Partners with college and foundation finance team members to ensure the integrity, accuracy, and consistency of financial reporting and internal controls across all assigned areas of responsibility. Required Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree or higher in Accounting, Finance, Business, or related financial field and five (5) years of accounting experience; OR Certified Public Accountant (CPA) and three (3) years of accounting experience. Skills and Knowledge: Ability to work collaboratively in a dynamic setting and an environment of constant growth and change. Ability to analyze and interpret complex data. Ability to research and prepare comprehensive reports. Ability to monitor and adhere to quality control standards. Ability to work at a rapid pace with numerous interruptions. Ability to cope with stressful conditions. Ability to demonstrate tact, versatility, and adaptability. Ability to demonstrate a high degree of self-motivation and directional initiative. Comprehensive knowledge of healthcare operations, including medical billing, credentialing, clinical workflows, healthcare finance, and healthcare management best practices. Preferred Qualifications: Certified Public Accountant. Advanced expertise in data analytics, including experience with various database systems, mining, reporting, and dashboard development. Background Investigation Statement: Prior to hiring, the final candidate(s) must successfully pass a pre-employment background investigation and information obtained from social media and other internet sources. A prior conviction reported as a result of the background investigation DOES NOT automatically disqualify a candidate from consideration for this position. A candidate with a prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags will receive an individualized review of the prior conviction or negative behavioral red flags before a hiring decision is made. Equal Employment Opportunity : The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to any legally protected basis and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. More information is available in the EEOC’s Know Your Rights: Workplace discrimination is illegal poster. The University of Alabama affirms its longstanding commitment to institutional neutrality, free speech, and academic freedom. Apply Now Please note- all Employment positions close at 10:55pm CST. Non-Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 3 days. Exempt positions are posted a minimum of 7 days. Faculty positions are posted a minimum of 30 days. Need help? Please email the Human Resources Department at hr@ua.edu or contact us by phone at (205)-348-7732. If you anticipate needing any type of accommodation to participate in any portion of the University's employment process, including completion of the online application process, please contact our office in advance of your participation or visit. Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Alabama is an Equal Employment/Equal Educational Opportunity Institution. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment or volunteer status without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, age, genetic or family medical history information, disability, protected veteran status, or any other legally protected basis, and will not be discriminated against because of their protected status. Applicants to and employees of this institution are protected under Federal law from discrimination on several bases. Pay Transparency Policy Statement The contractor will not discharge or in any other manner discriminate against employees or applicants because they have inquired about, discussed, or disclosed their own pay or the pay of another employee or applicant. However, employees who have access to the compensation information of other employees or applicants as a part of their essential job functions cannot disclose the pay of other employees or applicants to individuals who do not otherwise have access to compensation information, unless the disclosure is (a) in response to a formal complaint or charge, (b) in furtherance of an investigation, proceeding, hearing, or action, including an investigation conducted by the employer, or (c) consistent with the contractor’s legal duty to furnish information. Supplemental Links EEOC Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Polygraph Protection Act The University of Alabama Annual Campus Security and Fire Safety Report contains information on campus safety statistics as well as University Safety and Security Policies. The report is available online to view or print at safety.ua.edu . FOLLOW US Accessibility | Equal Opportunity | About This Site | Webmaster Copyright © 2021 The University of Alabama | Disclaimer | Privacy | Accessibility Candidate Details × This website uses cookies to collect information to improve your browsing experience. Please review our Privacy Statement for more information. I do not accept I accept"
